acceptance_criteria: "Required categories cannot disappear under top-k packing or a tiny token budget while the result remains sufficient; Empty, missing, unavailable, expired, conflicting and truncated are distinguishable; Two providers with divergent revisions cannot produce a falsely coherent result; Changing a dependency, policy, provider schema or validity boundary invalidates cached coverage; unchanged dependencies support a stable compact delta; High-ranking irrelevant content cannot displace mandatory decision evidence; Provider timeout/failure and inaccessible sources yield bounded safe receipts without information leakage; Tests cover concurrent mutation during assembly, strict versus best-effort consistency, tiny budgets, missing mandatory categories and changed decisions; SDK/CLI/MCP fixtures agree on sufficiency and receipts; packed consumers and small/large workspaces pass existing latency/token gates"
